---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/alternatives/privy-alternative';
const title = "Privy Alternatives for Shopify (2026)";
const desc = "Evaluate keeping Privy, moving sending or replacing capture with a concrete field, offer, identity and account-continuity handover.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Privy only a popup tool?",
    "answer": "No. Its current site markets email, SMS, segmentation, reporting and visual automation alongside list growth. Evaluate the functions available in your actual account rather than assuming it stops at basic welcome and cart reminders."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does the Sendlane acquisition require a migration?",
    "answer": "The announcement confirms the acquisition, not your account-specific cutover. Ask which account, contract, support arrangement and features apply before planning a move or buying a supposedly separate replacement."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I keep capture while moving email?",
    "answer": "Consider it if the supported integration and current plan meet the brief. Verify field mapping, list destination, disclosures, updates and offer delivery end to end before changing production ownership."
  },
  {
    "question": "How do I decide the handoff is complete?",
    "answer": "Record acceptance for new and returning signups, withdrawals, purchases, duplicate identities, offer delivery and old queues. Confirm account access and rollback procedures; neither a subscriber CSV nor a fixed watch period proves completion."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/alternatives">Alternatives</a></nav>
    <article class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">

      <h1>Privy alternatives for Shopify: decide which layer should move</h1>
      <p>Replacing an onsite offer is different from replacing its email delivery, SMS identity or account relationship. A merchant preparing a product drop needs the promised code to reach the right subscriber once, while a returning buyer's changed permission and purchase state reach the sender. Map that path before choosing another tool.</p>
      <h2>Start with current Privy, not an old feature ceiling</h2>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://www.privy.com/">Privy's current product site</a> presents targeted popups and quizzes, an email editor, segmentation, revenue reporting and a visual automation builder including welcome and winback. Those are positive reasons to evaluate keeping the account. They do not prove every requested workflow is included in your plan, but they contradict treating Privy as capture with only basic reminders.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://www.privy.com/sendlane-acquisition">Privy's Sendlane acquisition announcement</a> describes email, SMS and onsite marketing together. Ask your contact which interface, data store, agreement, support team and migration assistance apply to your current account. An unavailable app listing would not establish company shutdown; a failed help-page fetch would not establish a missing feature.</p>
      <h2>Choose the smallest useful change</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Keep and repair:</strong> retain working capture, reusable creative and familiar approvals if the live account can handle the required journeys. Diagnose an incorrectly mapped source field or inactive automation before paying to replace the whole stack.</li>
        <li><strong>Move sending:</strong> retain capture only if the supported destination integration and plan can deliver current fields, permission updates and offers reliably. Include both subscriptions and the integration owner in the cost.</li>
        <li><strong>Replace capture and sending:</strong> justified when a demonstrated targeting, identity or operating requirement cannot be met acceptably. Give forms, theme embeds, campaigns and delayed sends separate cutover tasks.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Candidate briefs with a practical benefit to demonstrate</h2>
      <p>Evaluate Justuno when the work is onsite targeting or collecting useful intent fields: ask it to recreate the actual display rules and downstream field contract. Evaluate Klaviyo when the work is maintaining event-driven profiles and segments: its <a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005080407">Shopify integration</a> is a concrete starting point for a data demonstration. These solve different jobs and need not both replace Privy.</p>
      <p>For Omnisend, request one coordinated email/SMS journey with your approval and suppression requirements. For an email-focused Sequenzy evaluation, demonstrate creating, approving and updating the actual sequence and its Shopify inputs. A simpler campaign operation can include Shopify's marketing tools in the evaluation. No candidate receives a default rank, a claimed speed advantage or assumed channel coverage from this shortlist; account-level acceptance decides.</p>
      <h2>Proposed capture, offer and identity handover fixture</h2>
      <p>Run this controlled exercise before changing the live theme. It describes proposed checks, not results. Use a product-page signup, exit-intent offer and returning subscriber on mobile and desktop. Include one changed email address, one phone number attached to an existing shopper, a withdrawn subscriber and a purchaser who returns to the offer.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Inventory every display.</strong> Save creative, targeting, device rules, exclusions, display frequency, dismissal behavior, translations, accessibility requirements and theme placement. Record whether a quiz answer is a profile field, tag or event; preserve its meaning and type at the destination.</li>
        <li><strong>Map the offer contract.</strong> Specify code generation, eligibility, expiration, usage and combination rules, destination URL, promised delivery channel and fallback. Check the actual Shopify discount configuration. A welcome email arriving without a usable code fails even if the contact sync succeeds.</li>
        <li><strong>Trace source to sender.</strong> Submit a controlled signup and compare form ID, source/campaign, disclosure version, timestamp, sender, purpose, channel and destination list ID. Retain current withdrawal and suppression state. A pre-existing address must not silently become a fresh subscription to every channel.</li>
        <li><strong>Reconcile identity updates.</strong> Define which system owns email, phone and customer ID changes. Try a repeated form submission, an address change and conflicting updates from Shopify and the capture tool. Expected behavior should prevent duplicate welcome offers and avoid merging unrelated shoppers.</li>
        <li><strong>Follow the purchase.</strong> Submit a cart event then purchase before its reminder. Delay the purchase update and replay the original event. Record the intended enrollment, current-state exit and deduplication behavior, including gift and open-support exclusions where the merchant uses them.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Hand over callers, creative and pending work</h2>
      <p>List theme embeds, checkout integrations, landing pages, QR links and external API callers that still write to the old account. Assign a new destination and credential owner to each. Save approved templates, product blocks, unsubscribe and preference links, branded domains and fallback text; check rendering with actual catalog content and expired offers.</p>
      <p>For SMS, confirm the number or sending identity arrangement, transfer eligibility, keyword destinations, reply inbox, escalation coverage and current channel permission. Email permission or a purchase does not authorize SMS. Check the destination's applicable timing and permission requirements and the account's ability to enforce them. Test the intended withdrawal and help-response paths before relying on them.</p>
      <p>Pause equivalent old automations and record whether pending messages will finish, cancel or be recreated once. Give the replacement one owner per trigger and purpose. Reconcile purchases and withdrawals immediately before dispatch, including changes made during import. Historical data should not enroll shoppers into a fresh offer accidentally. Choose channel spacing and frequency from the program promise and measured behavior, rather than an arbitrary twenty-four-hour rule.</p>
      <h2>Account continuity and rollback</h2>
      <p>Obtain the current account's export fields, access roles, billing owner, support contact, data retention and cancellation terms. Confirm which historical reports, consent evidence and creative can be retained. An acquisition announcement does not guarantee automatic data transfer, identical pricing or universal feature availability for every account.</p>
      <p>Keep a versioned copy of the old display configuration and a map of new signups during cutover. Rollback should disable replacement entry and queued sends, preserve new permission changes and purchases, and restore only approved old forms and actions. Reconcile the intervening records before restarting; do not reactivate all historical automations. Use delivery, bounce, complaint and engagement evidence to set any sender ramp.</p>
      <h2>Price the complete offer-to-order path</h2>
      <p>Request current quotes for the actual capture workload, billable contacts, normal and peak email volume, SMS destinations and message parts, carrier fees, support and onboarding. Compare keeping Privy with split capture/sending and full replacement. Include overlapping subscriptions, integration maintenance, creative rebuilding and staff time; a combined monthly total cannot be inferred from old entry prices.</p>
      <p>Illustrative contribution calculation: on a $100 order, $45 fixed goods cost and $10 other variable costs leave $45. A $25 offer leaves $20, not a newly reduced goods-cost estimate. Thirty incremental orders at $20 contribute $600; subtracting $450 for incremental platform and messaging cost leaves $150 before extra labor and returns. The offer is neither automatically profitable nor automatically loss-making. Check incrementality with an appropriate comparison and review full-price repeat purchase, opt-outs and offer redemption alongside attributed revenue.</p>
      <p>Related: <a class="link" href="/alternatives/klaviyo-alternative">Klaviyo alternatives</a> focuses on profile, segment and flow reconstruction. <a class="link" href="/compare/privy-vs-justuno">Privy vs Justuno</a> provides a separate capture comparison; <a class="link" href="/alternatives">all alternatives</a> lists other decision contexts.</p>
    </article>
  </div></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Privy alternatives FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
